    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and the suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the per-city owner cap rejecting creation with **409** when the owner's city already holds 50+ owners.\n\nTo keep structural impact low, I followed the codebase's existing pattern of small, cohesive static helpers (`HouseholdMatcher`, `NamesakeCounter`, `CustomerCodeGenerator`) that `addOwner` already delegates to:\n\n- **New file** `service/CityCapacity.java` \u2014 a tiny helper (`isFull`) with essentially no surrounding complexity (WMC_other \u2248 0), holding the `MAX_OWNERS_PER_CITY = 50` rule and a case-insensitive city count.\n- **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 added a single `if (CityCapacity.isFull(owners, owner)) return 409;` branch plus one import, mirroring the adjacent telephone/household conflict checks. The already-fetched `owners` collection is reused, so no extra data access.\n\nThis keeps the change in the large controller class to one simple branch (minimal changed lines, CC bump of +1), pushing the new logic into a class whose surrounding complexity is zero.\n\nTests: `mvnw test` \u2192 **BUILD SUCCESS**, `AcceptanceTest.coreRejectsWhenCityAtCapacity` passes (fill a fresh city to 50, 51st rejected with 409).",
